  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CA: FTFIL for Animal Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Bureau for Resilience and Food Security (RFS)):  Purpose: To implement the Science, Technology and Innovation elements of the Global Food Security Act, a portfolio of research programs across the biophysical and social sciences have been developed and are central to advancing novel solutions that support global efforts to reduce hunger, poverty, and malnutrition. This five-year program seeks to support research for technology development and testing of new, improved animal health interventions such as vaccines and diagnostic tests to improve the control of East Coast fever (ECF), a devastating disease of cattle. The program will also build the capacity of a local university to conduct laboratory-based animal health research and train a new generation of animal health scientists. The activity draws on the expertise of US universities and developing country research institutions to address the GFSS goal of reducing global hunger, malnutrition, and poverty. $1 million of funding within this IM contributes to meeting the required &quot;Research and Development&quot; directive of $148.8 million and the required &quot;Feed the Future Innovation Labs&quot; sub-directive of $58 million...Activities: The program will complete the equipping of the newly refurbished laboratory at the University of Nairobi in Kenya, engage in field-based and laboratory research to develop and innovate East Coast Fever diagnostic tools and vaccines for future scaling..Benefitting Countries: Kenya..</narrative>
  </description>
